<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Dividing a Class with Twins: Group Formation Challenge</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In how many ways can a class of \({@class_tot@}\) be divided into two groups of \({@group_1@}\) and \({@group_2@}\) respectively if the class contains one set of twins who must not be separated?</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>There are two options, depending on which group the twins are in:</p>
<p>If the twins are in the group of \({@group_2@}\), then there are \(^{@class_tot-2@} C_{@group_1@}\) ways of choosing the group of \({@group_1@}\) – the remaining \({@(class_tot-2)-group_1@}\) are put together with the twins.</p>
<p>If they are in the group of \({@group_1@}\), then there are \(^{@class_tot-2@} C_{@group_2@}\) ways of choosing the group of \({@group_2@}\) – the remaining \({@(class_tot-2)-group_2@}\) are put together with the twins.</p>
<p>Thus the number of possibilities is  \(^{@class_tot-2@} C_{@group_1@} + {}^{@class_tot-2@} C_{@group_2@} = {@ta@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
